{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LATE ADDITION — ticket-state drift observed during the closing verification sweep.\n\n858c read back as 'closed' despite having been reopened and re-verified earlier, with its rescoped description and both comments fully intact. The DESCRIPTION write survived; only the STATUS was reverted. Re-reopened and re-verified as open.\n\nThat asymmetry matters for diagnosis: it is a status-only overwrite, not a revision rollback, which points at inbound field-level reconciliation rather than an event-log or compaction fault. Jira still held the ticket closed from the earlier (superseded) close, and the Reconcile Bridge was re-enabled mid-session. Another agent independently reported 556a drifting open -> in_progress in the same window. Evidence recorded on 4136.\n\nVERIFICATION SWEEP RESULT: all other tickets touched this session read back in their intended states — 16 spot-checked closures all closed; 7084 in_progress with 11 comments; 2876/81d5/556a/8fbd/514d open with their decision comments; 9fb3 and 9f63 in_progress with their agents; 535e created as status=idea and linked discovered_from 7084. Session log is this ticket (f218-d02e-e4be-400d), two entries."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786121489058471001,"uuid":"618c9415-2278-49f8-bd9f-5302113aaba4"}